{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"09c236aab61d1e76634ebb0c80e05611f6879318c200c9827309986cd86890a1","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion-verification close gate","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/runaway_guard.py","src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py","ToolCallLedger","_memo_toolsets","_runaway_guard_toolsets","build_agent_kwargs","RunawayToolLoopError","read_file","distinct_ratio_window","completion_tool_policy.BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE","pai_tools._READ_MAX_LINES"],"problem_keywords":["completion verification","runaway tool loop","guard memoization conflict","tool call deduplication","agent loop","evidence verification"],"propositions":["The runaway guard counts memo-served cache hits as loop evidence because it sits outermost in the layer composition, observing all calls before the memo layer can serve them for free, causing legitimate repeated evidence reads to trip RunawayToolLoopError.","Reads past the cached window fall back to uncached exact-range reads, degrading the distinct-ratio further and increasing false-positive loop detection on legitimate verification patterns.","The composition Guard→Memo→Steering is immutable due to completion policy requiring visibility into all call attempts, preventing a simple layer reordering fix.","A deterministic evidence compilation and tool-free judgment model would eliminate the runaway loop entirely by removing the agent loop, making in-band guards unnecessary."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787527574527190001,"uuid":"ca67e0b5-5ee1-45ac-91e2-53e9bc53c6a0"}